# I03.var11 prospective contract-only lineage

Current contract draft: `tmp/i03-var11-prospective-contract-draft-v2-20261008.json`, 322,180 bytes, SHA-256 `0e5eb2b6f424faf1f4fe922c6c29adac2ac1b4db08d21a4cccf1d6fd14a4a709`. This is a **proposal for independent contract review**, not model construction, native approval, or behavioral acceptance. The package and unique run were absent at root selection and remained absent when the draft was created. The exact root selection receipt is `tmp/i03-var11-root-selection-proof-20261008/receipt.json`, 2,867 bytes, SHA-256 `085a3bab04216dd33730bc336de4fb22aa327a685ddac158327e8f0771dc0828`.

The accepted primary comparator is published I03.var02 idle-crew OUT v1.0.2 (index SHA-256 `4060de5d7434ff675949b9eea7fb8f827ac0c72a56e530169b60ecb0da0724dc`). Its source has one h6, quantity-one P-CREW OUT transfer with TFDT0, opening local quantity2 and a 36-hour horizon. The only proposed authored changes are PDESC and TFDT0→40 in that row. The proposed child has no evidence yet. I03.var06 v1.0.1 is a **published, bounded retrospective counterexample context** (index SHA-256 `b4e82d39d5780e3eb981a717a0c9b598489c62747e9acc1e5ab5bfeae4e9ffbb`): its original v1.0.0 native run with TFDT4 failed its prospective gate, while a separate read-only classification established unchanged raw printed4 at h6 and linked arrival h10. That failed native run is preserved as context, never promoted to an accepted parent.

The installed manual (SHA-256 `39427027c46809a9ce9ebcb9be04e7396d96746e42a6f8c7c0ba2ddc294ef8a3`) pp478–479 says TFDT is ignored for OUT transfers. The fixed TFDT4 witness conflicts with that description for its one row. The proposed TFDT40 hypothesis must therefore be tested directly: the native roundtrip retains 40, task0 starts with quantity1 and prints transfer time40 at h6, and no linked arrival/cancellation occurs through physical/log horizon h36. `6+40=46` is arithmetic **outside** the run, not an observed arrival. The contract classifies the derived started-but-unarrived OUT task quantity, not a persistent person or outside resource pool. A report transit display cannot be inferred from arrival absence; the report oracle remains source/event-derived with separately named bounded presentation fields.

The contract pins 452 primary/secondary published source files and indices as separate local and Git blob identities at base `50c552285f69e0b5a8bf82a8cdc6999b9e68f7cf`, plus 118 accepted/context original raw files and 26 excluded failed-witness run files. Installed executable, manual, dictionary and required repository docs have exact size/SHA pins. The current 492-entry catalog local CRLF bytes and base Git LF blob are distinct; later replay requires an exact owned historical archive plus type-exact live metadata and first492 entries. Parent I03.var02's 14,996 original versus 14,995 postappend reader count is historical publication context, not a waiver in the new contract. The separate I03.var06 reader has a stable 20,433 checks; no previous approval carries forward.

The full prospective gate remains independent: exact 32-table source and native export, complete typed event and quantity ledgers, all 5,210 expected cells per arm, predeclared exact half-hour/discrete/null and five exact binary32 resource means, semantic tamper rejections and separate source/raw custody. Only after fresh contract GO may an input, runner or checker be built; actual SSH5 pure preflight, new independent prelaunch approval and root-only unique native execution are later gates. There is no new native call in this contract stage.

The first TMP builder draft failed before writing a contract because it referenced a missing historical JSON key. Its source is preserved at `tmp/build-i03-var11-contract-draft-v1-failed-key-20261008.py.bytes` (SHA-256 `c708686f3d1d153a0fc8731e4877980089cc61043df1429ef65354c90ec29570`); the original stderr was only shown in the tool transcript, so no output-byte claim is made. Contract draft v1 remains preserved at `tmp/i03-var11-prospective-contract-draft-v1-20261008.json` (320,645 bytes, SHA-256 `01a21672d6f48cdaff6f3d871b73694d804a9361e4c202d0849101654d6f9ebe`). Draft v2 corrects h6 wording: the accepted log prints creation, demand and task start in order; local/nominal decrements are derived from task and result states, not separately printed decrement lines.
